      "content": "To teach that algorithms are not neutral, show students how historical biases in training data—such as past home value records created through redlining—become embedded code that perpetuates denial of loans to racialized communities. Demonstrate this concretely by running a simulation where two applicants with identical incomes are judged differently solely because their zip codes reflect historical racial segregation. Emphasize that \"objective\" math simply reflects the flawed reality it was built to measure, turning historical discrimination into a self-reinforcing digital loop. This reframes the lesson from technical error to intentional structural design where data science tools amplify existing societal inequalities.",
